{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>For there is</b> a man who labors with worldly matters in his great wisdom and attains the desire of his heart that he pursued, and another man who did not labor for it — his portion will be given to him. This is the matter mentioned above, that I labored and grew wise under the sun. Know that the word חכמתי is of the intransitive verbs, and its meaning is: I labored in wisdom. And he who inherits him takes everything without labor. And it is possible that the word יתננו is like יתן לו (he will give him), for it is a verb that takes two objects, and like it: כי ארץ הנגב נתתני (for the land of the Negev you have given me [Judges 1:15]). And the meaning of חלקו (his portion) is the portion that fell to his lot from heaven, as our predecessors of blessed memory said: children, life, and sustenance."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:09.831794694Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}